# D Flip-Flop

## Goal

Learn how to implement a D Flip-Flop in Verilog and understand how sequential logic stores data using a clock signal.

## Concepts Learned

- module
- input
- output
- reg/logic
- always block
- posedge
- clock
- reset
- sequential logic

## Truth Table

| Reset | Clock | D | Q (Next) |
|:-----:|:-----:|:-:|:--------:|
|   1   |   ↑   | X |    0     |
|   0   |   ↑   | 0 |    0     |
|   0   |   ↑   | 1 |    1     |
|   0   | No ↑  | X | Holds Q  |

> **↑** = Rising edge of the clock  
> **X** = Don't care / any value

